{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyONC3KyCXL4aB1cxi2iEh6N"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["1. Background\n","An Electric Vehicle (EV) company is testing the performance of a new battery system. During the test, sensors\n","collect information about the battery at different time intervals.\n","The following parameters are monitored:\n","● Temperature (°C)\n","● Voltage (V)\n","● Current (A)\n","● Battery Charge (%)\n","The company wants to analyze the collected data and determine whether the battery is operating safely and\n","efficiently.\n","You are appointed as a Battery Data Analytics Team. Analyze the data using Python, NumPy, Linear Algebra,\n","and Calculus.\n","2. Battery Sensor Data\n","The following readings were collected during a 6-hour test:\n","Time (h) Temperature (°C) Voltage (V) Current (A) Charge (%)\n","0 32 400 20 95\n","1 35 395 22 88\n","2 38 390 25 80\n","3 40 385 28 70\n","4 42 380 30 60\n","5 45 375 32 48\n","\n","Task 1 — Analysis Using Python Basics\n","Store the given sensor readings using appropriate Python data structures, then perform the following tasks.\n","1. Display the sensor readings\n","Use a for loop to display all battery readings."],"metadata":{"id":"wTADPPI0-tj5"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Battery Sensor Data\n","battery_data = [\n","    (0, 32, 400, 20, 95),\n","    (1, 35, 395, 22, 88),\n","    (2, 38, 390, 25, 80),\n","    (3, 40, 385, 28, 70),\n","    (4, 42, 380, 30, 60),\n","    (5, 45, 375, 32, 48)\n","]\n","\n","# Display all battery readings using a for loop\n","print(\"Battery Sensor Readings\")\n","print(\"-\" * 60)\n","\n","for time, temperature, voltage, current, charge in battery_data:\n","    print(\n","        f\"Time: {time} h | \"\n","        f\"Temperature: {temperature} °C | \"\n","        f\"Voltage: {voltage} V | \"\n","        f\"Current: {current} A | \"\n","        f\"Charge: {charge}%\"\n","    )"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"r7oEiTl5_PAQ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958365396,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"72e8e47a-2042-46f8-dcf6-70de2a6b22c0"},"execution_count":4,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Battery Sensor Readings\n","------------------------------------------------------------\n","Time: 0 h | Temperature: 32 °C | Voltage: 400 V | Current: 20 A | Charge: 95%\n","Time: 1 h | Temperature: 35 °C | Voltage: 395 V | Current: 22 A | Charge: 88%\n","Time: 2 h | Temperature: 38 °C | Voltage: 390 V | Current: 25 A | Charge: 80%\n","Time: 3 h | Temperature: 40 °C | Voltage: 385 V | Current: 28 A | Charge: 70%\n","Time: 4 h | Temperature: 42 °C | Voltage: 380 V | Current: 30 A | Charge: 60%\n","Time: 5 h | Temperature: 45 °C | Voltage: 375 V | Current: 32 A | Charge: 48%\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["2. Identify high temperature\n","Apply the following condition:\n","\n","If T &gt; 40 °C\n","\n","Display: “High Temperature Alert”\n","Otherwise, display: “Temperature Normal”"],"metadata":{"id":"RdXXUD_6_XA4"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Identify high temperature\n","\n","for time, temperature, voltage, current, charge in battery_data:\n","    if temperature > 40:\n","        print(f\"Time {time} h: High Temperature Alert\")\n","    else:\n","        print(f\"Time {time} h: Temperature Normal\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"oq52-1bA_X2Q","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958377250,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":45,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"04e681da-1bd0-440a-e331-80c527e00bf0"},"execution_count":5,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Time 0 h: Temperature Normal\n","Time 1 h: Temperature Normal\n","Time 2 h: Temperature Normal\n","Time 3 h: Temperature Normal\n","Time 4 h: High Temperature Alert\n","Time 5 h: High Temperature Alert\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["3. Identify low battery\n","Apply the following condition:\n","\n","If C &lt; 50 %\n","\n","Display: “Low Battery Alert”\n","Otherwise, display: “Battery Charge Normal”"],"metadata":{"id":"b_N5g4_D_Zzo"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Identify low battery\n","\n","for time, temperature, voltage, current, charge in battery_data:\n","    if charge < 50:\n","        print(f\"Time {time} h: Low Battery Alert\")\n","    else:\n","        print(f\"Time {time} h: Battery Charge Normal\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"6e8iDST5_dEQ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958380383,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":8,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"8c8a5a41-daba-4f77-ff9f-6472f1f15268"},"execution_count":6,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Time 0 h: Battery Charge Normal\n","Time 1 h: Battery Charge Normal\n","Time 2 h: Battery Charge Normal\n","Time 3 h: Battery Charge Normal\n","Time 4 h: Battery Charge Normal\n","Time 5 h: Low Battery Alert\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["4. Create a function\n","Create a function battery_status(charge) that returns a status based on:\n","High, C &gt; 70\n","Status = Medium, 50 ≤ C ≤ 70\n","Low, C &lt; 50"],"metadata":{"id":"T4JolSEt_fR6"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Create a function to determine battery status\n","\n","def battery_status(charge):\n","    if charge > 70:\n","        return \"High\"\n","    elif 50 <= charge <= 70:\n","        return \"Medium\"\n","    else:\n","        return \"Low\"\n","\n","\n","# Test the function using the battery data\n","for time, temperature, voltage, current, charge in battery_data:\n","    print(f\"Time {time} h | Charge: {charge}% | Status: {battery_status(charge)}\")"],"metadat