ery readings (C < 50%):\")\n","print(low_battery)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"sw9e-JQrAMth","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958404969,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"f5adfd5c-e3a3-4bf6-ebd8-ac3830f35cb2"},"execution_count":13,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Low-battery readings (C < 50%):\n","[[ 45 375  32  48]]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Task 3 — Analysis Using Linear Algebra\n","The company uses temperature and current to calculate a simplified Battery Stress Index.\n","Let the transformation matrix be:\n","\n","┌ 2 1 ┐\n","A = │ │\n","└ 1 3 ┘\n","\n","Consider the sensor input:\n","\n","┌ T ┐ ┌ 40 ┐\n","X = │ │ = │ │\n","└ I ┘ └ 25 ┘\n","\n","The output is calculated as:\n","\n","Y = A X\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","┌ 2 1 ┐ ┌ 40 ┐\n","Y = │ │ × │ │\n","└ 1 3 ┘ └ 25 ┘\n","\n","Students must calculate the resulting vector Y.\n","Additional Linear Algebra Tasks\n","For the matrix A above, find:\n","1. Transpose\n","\n","Battery Data Analytics — Case Study Assignment\n","\n","Page 4 of 2\n","Aᵀ"],"metadata":{"id":"s_PJ1Dc2AUDA"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","\n","# Transformation matrix\n","A = np.array([\n","    [2, 1],\n","    [1, 3]\n","])\n","\n","# Sensor input [Temperature, Current]\n","X = np.array([\n","    [40],\n","    [25]\n","])\n","\n","# Calculate Y = AX\n","Y = A @ X\n","\n","print(\"Y =\")\n","print(Y)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"Tst8UhHXAUuI","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958408283,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":19,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"05483cc0-fb6b-4c16-c6d5-55abc17d861b"},"execution_count":14,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Y =\n","[[105]\n"," [115]]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["2. Determinant\n","\n","det(A)"],"metadata":{"id":"KjCEziwCAXJQ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Calculate determinant of A\n","det_A = np.linalg.det(A)\n","\n","print(\"Determinant of A:\", det_A)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"STibe2ILAbgg","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958412649,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":21,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"d26014a9-71a1-453f-832c-82649c0dce51"},"execution_count":15,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Determinant of A: 5.000000000000001\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["3. Inverse\n","A⁻¹, if the inverse exists."],"metadata":{"id":"uxrR33i4Adwg"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Find the inverse of A\n","if np.linalg.det(A) != 0:\n","    A_inverse = np.linalg.inv(A)\n","    print(\"Inverse of A:\")\n","    print(A_inverse)\n","else:\n","    print(\"Inverse does not exist.\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"nEnF8g7PAkMp","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958418473,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":15,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"54f70c33-34bb-4caa-b3d8-596e67cf5421"},"execution_count":16,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Inverse of A:\n","[[ 0.6 -0.2]\n"," [-0.2  0.4]]\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Solving a System of Equations\n","The engineers need to determine two unknown battery parameters x and y. The equations are:\n","\n","2x + y = 100\n","x + 3y = 120\n","\n","Write the equations in matrix form:\n","\n","A X = B\n","\n","where:\n","\n","┌ 2 1 ┐ ┌ x ┐ ┌ 100 ┐\n","A = │ │ X = │ │ B = │ │\n","└ 1 3 ┘ └ y ┘ └ 120 ┘\n","\n","Students must solve for x and y using NumPy."],"metadata":{"id":"-LpUKXpdAmbw"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","\n","# Matrix A\n","A = np.array([\n","    [2, 1],\n","    [1, 3]\n","])\n","\n","# Matrix B\n","B = np.array([\n","    100,\n","    120\n","])\n","\n","# Solve AX = B\n","X = np.linalg.solve(A, B)\n","\n","print(\"Solution:\")\n","print(X)\n","\n","print(\"x =\", X[0])\n","print(\"y =\", X[1])"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"VABvb_qUAsoZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958421523,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"d7cd9ebf-e646-422e-d813-e78741fedeea"},"execution_count":17,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Solution:\n","[36. 28.]\n","x = 36.0\n","y = 28.0\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Task 4 — Analysis Using Calculus\n","The battery charge is modeled as a function of time:\n","\n","C(t) = 100 − 2t − ½t²\n","where C(t) is the battery charge percentage and t is the time in hours.\n","1. Find the rate of change of battery charge\n","The rate at which the battery charge changes is given by dC/dt. Differentiate C(t) and determine dC/dt."],"metadata":{"id":"pDYCTwOpAvxI"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import sympy as sp\n","\n","t = sp.symbols('t')\n","\n","# Battery charge function\n","C = 100 - 2*t - sp.Rational(1, 2)*t**2\n","\n","# Differentiate\n","dC_dt = sp.diff(C, t)\n","\n","print(\"C(t) =\", C)\n","print(\"dC/dt =\", dC_dt)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"tN9mEEKsAz3x","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958428182,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":3194,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"86584a0b-94d0-4f8e-8478-19b696932f27"},"execution_count":18,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["C(t) = -t**2/2 - 2*t + 100\n","dC/dt = -t - 2\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["2. Calculate the discharge rate\n","Find the discharge rate at t = 2 and t = 5, that is, calculate:\n","\n","dC/dt at t = 2 and dC/dt at t = 5"],"metadata":{"id":"9wCSBg4rA3XK"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Calculate discharge rate at t = 2 and t = 5\n","\n","rate_at_2 = dC_dt.subs(t, 2)\n","rate_at_5 = dC_dt.subs(t, 5)\n","\n","print(\"dC/dt at t = 2:\", rate_at_2, \"% per hour\")\n","print(\"dC/dt at t = 5:\", rate_at_5, \"% per hour\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"S35gU8JYA-ax","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958430041,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"b77e33a9-c9c2-4dff-fd08-c9b05699a379"},"execution_count":19,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["dC/dt at t = 2: -4 % per hour\n","dC/dt at t = 5: -7 % per hour\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["3. Interpret the result\n","Based on the values of dC/dt, determine whether the battery is losing charge:\n","● At a constant rate\n","● At an increasing rate\n","● At a decreasing rate"],"metadata":{"id":"vJvNwU_tBA-5"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Task 4.3 — Interpret the discharge rate\n","\n","# Rates calculated earlier\n","rate_at_2 = dC_dt.subs(t, 2)\n","rate_at_5 = dC_dt.subs(t, 5)\n","\n","print(\"Rate at t = 2:\", rate_at_2)\n","print(\"Rate at t = 5:\", rate_at_5)\n","\n","# Interpret the result\n","if abs(rate_at_5) > abs(rate_at_2):\n","    print(\"The battery is losing charge at an increasing rate.\")\n","elif abs(rate_at_5) < abs(rate_at_2):\n","    print(\"The battery is losing charge at a decreasing rate.\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"The battery is losing charge at a constant rate.\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"wFElcbGABFBZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786958433017,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":13,"user":{"displayName":"PASARTHI SANJANA","userId":"13386261391473761518"}},"outputId":"7ad3a2bf-4797-46ab-c86e-a95d71932d20"},"execution_count":20,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Rate at t = 2: -4\n","Rate at t = 5: -7\n","The battery is losing charge at an increasing rate.\n"]}]}]}